caption: JavaScript transforms
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/custom-transforms [[Transforms Guide]]
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/custom-transforms/js
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

`type: application/javascript`.  The body is a //function body// (not a
function expression).  In scope: `value`; `params`, the bracketed
parameters as an array of strings (`{{x|year-bucket[10]}}` gives
`['10']`); `record`, the whole current record; and `counter`, the
record's position counting from 1.  Whatever you `return` becomes the
transformed value:

```
title: Year Bucket
name: year-bucket
tags: $:/tags/json-convert/transform
type: application/javascript

const n = Number(value)
if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return ''
return String(Math.floor(n / 10) * 10) + 's'
```

A `2007` input becomes `"2000s"`.  Read `params[0]` to make the bucket
width a parameter, and `record.someOtherField` when the result depends
on more than the one value.

''Errors.''  If the body fails to compile (`SyntaxError`), the transform is
skipped entirely — using it in a profile produces ''unknown-transform''.  If
it throws at run time, the affected token resolves to the empty string but
the conversion continues.
